2. Free noncommercial research permission

Each rights holder offering the Software under this license grants you a
worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, run, copy,
inspect, modify and redistribute the Software and modifications solely for
noncommercial research, reproduction and evaluation. No individual permission
request or payment is required for these permitted activities.

Keep existing copyright, attribution and license notices. Include this license
with redistributed copies, identify your modifications, and distribute the
Software and modifications under these same terms. Publication of research
findings is permitted, including in commercially published scholarly journals;
such publication does not itself constitute commercial use of the Software.

3. Commercial use requires a separate agreement

The permission above does not cover activities undertaken for commercial
advantage, including commercial deployment, commercial product or service
development, commercial research and development, paid services using the
Software, or using the Software to train models intended for commercial use.
An academic or nonprofit affiliation does not by itself make such activities
noncommercial.

Before undertaking commercial use, obtain a separate written agreement from
the relevant rights holder or an authorized representative. Any fees or
royalties must be negotiated and specified in that agreement; this license
does not impose an automatic fee or royalty obligation. Commercial licensing
enquiries may be directed to hongwei.ma@sydney.edu.au.

4. Patent rights

If a rights holder offering the Software under this license controls patent
claims necessarily practiced by a permitted noncommercial use of the Software,
